[REPORT]
; Nodes: below the R1 outlet main (n303), the largest turbidity responses
; (n52, n412, n407, n56), a node fed by low-shear pipes (n4) and the tank T1.
; Links: 200 mm mains with the highest shear (p227, the R1 outlet, exceeds the
; 1.8 Pa ultimate strength and is scoured clean; p477), 100 mm pipes that
; mobilise (p69, p105, p483) and a 100 mm pipe that only regenerates (p4).
; Link TURB is the pipe average after advection: in short, fast pipes such as
; p227 (residence time < 60 s) it shows the inflow value; the material shows
; up at the downstream node.
; MSX appends /L to bulk and /M2 to wall units in the report: TURB is NTU,
; CPOT TPMU/m2, and TCOND and TAPP are in Pa.
  NODES   n303 n52 n412 n407 n56 n4 T1
  LINKS   p227 p477 p69 p105 p483 p4
  SPECIES TURB  YES 3
  SPECIES CPOT  YES 5
  SPECIES TCOND YES 4
